   "widgets_values": [
    "## Script length ↔ clip length\n\nEach S2V chunk is **77 frames ≈ 5 s** of video at 16 fps and consumes the next 5 s of speech.\n\nMeasured speaking rate of this voice: **English ≈ 2.5 words/s, Spanish ≈ 2.1 words/s**.\n\n| Chunks on | Video | English script | Spanish script |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 (groups 05 + 06 bypassed) | 5 s | ≤ 12 words | ≤ 10 words |\n| 2 (group 06 bypassed) | 10 s | ≤ 24 words | ≤ 20 words |\n| **3 (shipped)** | **15 s** | **≤ 35 words** | **≤ 30 words** |\n\n- Speech **longer** than the chunks is **cut off** at the end of the video (a 36-word Spanish line = 16.9 s lost its last 2 s).\n- Speech **shorter** leaves a silent tail where the character idles — bypass a chunk.\n- Check the length of `talk/voice_*.mp3` (saved first) if in doubt.\n- To go past 15 s, copy group 06, wire its `video_latent` / `samples1` from the previous\n  chunk's **Append** output, and point the first-frame fix (node 29/30) at the new last Append.\n\n## Languages\n\nThe TTS node's `language` is **Auto**: write the SCRIPT in English or Spanish and it is\ndetected. If a Spanish line comes out with an English accent (or vice-versa), set it to\n`Spanish` / `English` explicitly. Qwen3-TTS also speaks ZH, JA, KO, FR, DE, PT, RU, IT.\nThe Voice line stays in English either way — it describes the timbre, not the language."
   ],
   "title": "SCRIPT LENGTH & LANGUAGES — read before editing the SCRIPT"
  },
